    "tree": {
      "sha": "dbd429fabce6e6c9be47ba27e5599f9af658e8a8",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jphacks/tkb_2615/git/trees/dbd429fabce6e6c9be47ba27e5599f9af658e8a8"
    },
    "message": "Skip re-validating just-captured checkpoints and re-checking stored chunks\n\nLate in a run each save still validated the same freshly captured\ncheckpoint twice and ran the privacy regexes over the whole history.\nTimelineStore.record now saves through save_captured_branch, which uses\nthe checkpoint capture() just validated without another validation or\ndeep copy; save_branch keeps validating every other input.\n\nThe privacy check moves into the archive: it runs on chunk values that\nare not stored yet and on the field names of split objects. Stored\nchunks passed it when first written. New chunks are staged and written\nonly after every check passes, so a rejected checkpoint writes nothing,\nand saved manifests and chunks stay byte-identical.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
